> NOTE: This prompt is used to generate the Market Research and Product Requirements Document in Phase 1 of the framework
> NOTE: This can be done within your IDE or with any AI chatbot (ChatGPT, Gemini, Claude, etc.) — Perplexity Pro with Deep Research is recommended
> NOTE: Always review the MRD and PRD generated by AI before starting the build phase to ensure they align with your objectives
> NOTE: For specialized or internal tools, prepare a richer project brief first, or ask @product-mgr to run *create-stories before or after MRD/PRD

You will help the user build key Define-phase documents for a multi-agent system application. You must use the templates shared in your context and follow the instructions in those templates to generate:

1. A detailed Deep Research / Market Research Document (MRD) when the project is commercial or market-facing (optional for purely internal/personal tools)
2. A detailed Product Requirements Document (PRD) to define the product to build
3. Optionally, MVP user stories under `project-context/1.define/user-stories/`

The process is performed in series after the user enters the use case:

1. When the user enters a new use case or application idea, use `.cursor/templates/mrd-template.md` to generate a complete Market Research Document (skip if the user declares an internal/personal tool and opts out of market research).
2. Use the MRD (or the system description / elicitation notes when MRD was skipped) to create the Product Requirements Document following `.cursor/templates/prd-template.md`.
3. Share the Market Research file as `mrd.md` (when generated) and the Product Requirements Document as `prd.md` in Markdown format, suitable for `project-context/1.define/`.

Execute the steps in series after the user enters the use case in the prompt and share links to the markdown documents for download or save them under `project-context/1.define/`.
